      <variable ident="150" type="single">
        <name>AIUse</name>
        <label>Which of the following best describes how AI tools or agents are used at your organization today?</label>
        <position start="150" />
        <values>
          <value code="1">AI use is mostly optional and left up to individuals</value>
          <value code="2">Some teams actively encourage AI use, but practices vary across the organization</value>
          <value code="3">My organization provides approved AI tools and guidance for how to use them</value>
          <value code="4">My organization expects some employees to use AI tools for certain types of work</value>
          <value code="5">My organization measures or evaluates AI use as part of employee or team performance</value>
          <value code="6">My organization does not currently use AI tools or agents for work</value>
          <value code="7">Not sure</value>
          <value code="8">NA</value>
        </values>
      </variable>
      <variable ident="151" type="single">
        <name>AIAvoid</name>
        <label>Do you try to avoid using AI tools or agents at work or school? Select the option below that most accurately reflects your reasoning.</label>
        <position start="151" />
        <values>
          <value code="1">Environmental concerns</value>
          <value code="2">Concern over losing job skills or training an AI to replace you</value>
          <value code="3">Issues with privacy or security</value>
          <value code="4">Moral or ethical concerns</value>
          <value code="5">Difficulty or lack of training</value>
          <value code="6">I do not avoid using AI at work or school</value>
          <value code="7">Other, please specify:</value>
          <value code="8">NA</value>
        </values>
      </variable>
      <variable ident="152" type="single">
        <name>AITry</name>
        <label>Which of the following best describes how your organization currently approaches AI tools or models?</label>
        <position start="152" />
        <values>
          <value code="1">We mostly use one approved tool or model</value>
          <value code="2">We use a few approved tools or models</value>
          <value code="3">Different teams choose their own tools or models</value>
          <value code="4">We are trying multiple tools or models before deciding what to use longer-term</value>
          <value code="5">We are building internal tools or models</value>
          <value code="6">We are not using AI tools or models in a meaningful way</value>
          <value code="7">Not sure</value>
          <value code="8">NA</value>
        </values>
      </variable>
      <variable ident="153" type="multiple">
        <name>AIAdopt</name>
        <label>When you or your organization decides whether to adopt, continue using, or expand use of an AI tool or model for your work, which factors matter most? Select up to 3.</label>
        <position start="153" />
        <values>
          <value code="1">The tool produces useful and accurate results</value>
          <value code="2">The tool works well with how people already do their jobs</value>
          <value code="3">The tool meets security, privacy requirements</value>
          <value code="4">The tool meets legal or compliance requirements</value>
          <value code="5">The price is acceptable for the value it provides</value>
          <value code="6">The tool is worth paying more for because of better results</value>
          <value code="7">Usage and spending are easy to monitor or limit</value>
          <value code="8">The tool connects with systems people already use</value>
          <value code="9">The organization can switch tools or models without major disruption</value>
          <value code="10">Employees or teams are asking to use it</value>
          <value code="11">There is evidence that the tool improves business outcomes</value>
          <value code="12">The tool reduces time spent correcting, retrying, or reworking outputs</value>
          <value code="13">The tool has observability already integrated or built in</value>
          <value code="14">Review burden is low</value>
          <value code="15">Human oversight is manageable</value>
          <value code="16">Your company policy allows for usage</value>
          <value code="17">Not sure</value>
          <value code="18">Other, please specify</value>
          <value code="19">NA</value>
        </values>
      </variable>
      <variable ident="154" type="multiple">
        <name>AIToken</name>
        <label>Which, if any, of the following has your organization done related to AI tool or model usage? Select all that apply.</label>
        <position start="154" />
        <values>
          <value code="1">Set limits on who can use certain AI tools or models</value>
          <value code="2">Set limits on AI tool or model usage or spending</value>
          <value code="3">Reviewed internal usage or spending data for AI tools or models</value>
          <value code="4">Approved different AI tools or models for different types of work</value>
          <value code="5">Compared buying an AI tool with building something internally</value>
          <value code="6">Stopped using or reduced spending on other software tools while increasing investment in AI tools or models</value>
          <value code="7">Negotiated shorter commitments or the ability to switch AI tools or models over time</value>
          <value code="8">Increased spending on AI tools or models because results justified it</value>
          <value code="9">None of the above</value>
          <value code="10">Not sure</value>
          <value code="11">NA</value>
        </values>
      </variable>
      <variable ident="155" type="multiple">
